[36m(main_task pid=77121)[0m <information>Doc 1(Title: "Navroz") Navroz or Nowruz is the Avestan language term for the Persian New Year, which marks the beginning of spring and is also considered the New Year in the Persian calendar. The festival is celebrated on the day of the vernal equinox, around March 20 or 21. Navroz is an ancient festival and is a significant celebration in Iran, Afghanistan, Tajikistan, and Turkmenistan. It also holds importance in Pakistan, India, Nepal, Syria, Georgia, and the Kurdish regions of Turkey, Iraq, and North Africa. Celebrations include cleaning the home, spring-cleaning, buying new clothes, and decorating homes with flowers, especially tulips and hyacinths, to welcome the spring season. Navroz is a family-oriented holiday, with many people gathering with their relatives and loved ones to mark the occasion.</information>
