[36m(main_task pid=77121)[0m Following his time at Wabash College, Roberts pursued a career in law. He studied under Benjamin Hunter, who became the first judge of the Court of General Quarter Sessions of the Peace for Madison County, Indiana. Roberts was admitted to the bar and established a law practice in Worthington, Ohio.
