[36m(main_task pid=77121)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=77121)[0m In 1845, Roberts moved to Indian Territory, which is now Oklahoma, where he began practicing law and working with the Choctaw and Delaware tribes. He was appointed as a treaty commissioner for the Choctaw and Delaware tribes, and he also served as a delegate to the constitutional convention of the Chickasaw Nation in 1854.
