[36m(main_task pid=77121)[0m  ><think>Based on this information, it is clear that the asthenosphere is a weak, ductile part of the upper mantle where plate tectonic movements occur. The lithosphere-asthenosphere boundary separates the rigid upper crust and mantle from the weak, less viscous asthenosphere. This boundary is generally located around km below the surface. The asthenosphere is important in the process of plate tectonics and partial melting that leads to the formation of oceanic and continental crust.</think><answer>Lithosphere is the outermost layer of the Earth, comprising the crust and the upper part of the mantle. It is a rigid layer that helps to support the weight of the atmosphere and is divided into several plates. The asthenosphere is a weaker, more ductile layer located below the lithosphere and is critical for plate tectonic movements and the formation of new crust at mid-ocean ridges and for the recycling of the crust at subduction zones.</answer>
