[36m(main_task pid=77121)[0m Doc 3(Title: Äppeltig) Äppeltig () is a year-round product from the producer "Äppelbarbarna" (apple boys) from the village of Östra Fogelvik in the county of Småland in Sweden. The recipe and marketing of the product are based on those of the producer "Äppelbarbarna" that is owned and managed by the farmer Pär Johansson and the family of the inventor Elias Eriksson, the organisation Arat Svenska, Bernt Östberg and Cecilia Erlandsson. Before the relaunch of Äppeltig in October 2018, it had disappeared from the market after years of not being sold for reasons not given. "Äppelbarbarna" describes their Äppeltig as "a gluten-free, low in fat and low in sugar, handmade meat-free cake with thin rounds of mild apple". It has been said that this cake, if old enough, almost tastes like apples directly from the apple tree, thanks to a method of production, the "sweating" of the fruit, which concentrates the flavor and sugar of the apples. New packs of Äppeltig include a glue with various tips for various purposes (cake tin, pan, shortings...) depending on the main objectives of the consumer. "Äppelbarbarna" sells Äppeltig as a dessert, tea, and coffee and shops. It is now being sold throughout the country as a small cake (15x3x1.5 cm) with 4 to 6 apple slices.
